  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Hebrew UI Architecture**\n\nI\'m now diving into the UI architecture itself. I need a plan to encompass RTL support, a clean aesthetic, high contrast for readability, and responsiveness across all devices. I\'m thinking of tabbed or unified branches for different components and a live engine inspector for debugging. I want this Hebrew UI to be truly comprehensive and beautiful.\n\n\n**Defining Context States**\n\nI\'ve been working on the PantryContext, creating state for inventory, shopping lists, dishes, history logs, and more. Key functions include an engine command executor that updates data based on API calls, and a comprehensive set of functions to manage inventory mutations, stock changes, adding/deleting items, and cooking dishes, all updating relevant states.\n\n\n**Implementing Inventory Functions**\n\nI\'ve added functions to the PantryContext. I now have `moveShoppingItemToInventory` for stock conversion, `generateZeroWasteRecipes` to call the `/api/engine/zero-waste-recipes` endpoint, and `resetToMockData` for quick data resets. I\'m focusing on seamless inventory management.\n\n\n**Constructing Branch Views**\n\nI\'m now putting together the pantry view components. I am prioritizing utility drawer categorization with nested organization for easy access, including sections for packing supplies, fresh/refrigerated items, and garden herbs. Inventory summary stats will be displayed alongside slot cards, featuring progress bars, unit badges, and quick buttons. I\'ve also implemented filtering and search functionality for specific slots or keywords.\n\n\n\n**Developing Analytics Dashboard**\n\nI\'m now building out the analytical component. I\'m focusing on market search queries with copy and direct search buttons for efficiency. There is budget summaries by department and I have a component dedicated for expense breakdown. I\'m also planning to incorporate depletion velocity forecasts, predicting product exhaustion. Finally, I\'m working on waste prevention metrics for the dashboard.\n\n\n**Analyzing Stock Interactions**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating new stock data. I\'ve initiated actions based on a recent supermarket receipt (\"\327\242\327\234\327\220\327\252 \327\247\327\221\327\234\327\252 \327\241\327\225\327\244\327\250 \327\251\327\225\327\244\327\250\327\241\327\234\"), and I\'m generating queries for lunch recipes using available items (\"\327\236\327\224 \327\220\327\244\327\251\327\250 \327\234\327\224\327\233\327\231\327\237\"). I\'m developing synchronized shopping list features and implementing inventory-based waste reduction insights. Also, I\'m working on a live inspector panel.\nI\'m including dynamic actions with visual feedback, a structured payload in JSON, and an interactive command simulator, for direct input from the user. I\'m building a stock movement modal for adding receipts, allowing camera capture, image upload, text paste, and voice input.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 12
      nanos: 667622805
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
