  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Inventory Structure**\n\nI\'m currently focused on streamlining the inventory management in the \"Inventory Branch.\" I\'m working to simplify unit management by strictly utilizing base units. The approach also focuses on item details, and aims to include a drawer or modal, keeping in mind user-defined preferences for presentation. I\'m exploring how to present product details in a concise yet informative way.\n\n\n**Refining Packaging Units**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the simplification of unit management within the inventory. My current focus is to ensure that all initial inventory items use clean, integer packaging counts, such as whole numbers of jars or boxes. The unit type will also need to support Hebrew packaging units, like \"\327\246\327\240\327\246\327\240\327\252\". Additionally, stepper buttons will increment and decrement inventory by one package at a time. I\'m also planning the item detail modal/drawer.\n\n\n**Developing Inventory Details**\n\nI\'m now integrating crucial item-specific details. I\'m focusing on expiry status, incorporating indicators for close dates or validity, along with the option for short notes or location details. I\'m also planning a fast action button to add items directly to a shopping list, customizable by quantity. Direct buttons for notes editing or status markers (IN_STOCK, LOW, EMPTY) are also underway. Finally, I\'m including direct delete or close options.\n\n\n\n**Decomposing Recipes & Inventory**\n\nI\'m now focusing on recipe management. My key approach will be natural language input for recipes. Each dish will decompose into specific packaging units like \"1 \327\227\327\221\327\231\327\234\327\252 \327\230\327\225\327\244\327\225\" or \"2 \327\231\327\227\' \327\242\327\222\327\221\327\240\327\231\327\225\327\252.\" I will provide an instant visual breakdown, checking if each ingredient exists with its physical slot and available quantity, or marking it as missing with shopping list options.\n\n**Finalizing Recipe Handling**\n\nI\'m now working on the \"Finish Cooking\" functionality. A single button press will decrease inventory based on used units, updating statuses like IN_STOCK to LOW or EMPTY. I will maintain a clear history log, and will provide clear feedback.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 12135337
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
