  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Shopping Branch**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the \"Shopping Branch\" and its split-screen display requirements. Specifically, I\'m focusing on the necessity of a clear side-by-side or split-view interface across desktop and mobile. I\'m prioritizing the structure and visual distinction of the two key areas.\n\n\n**Refining Shopping List**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of the active shopping checklist. I\'m focusing on the integration of features like V-marking for completed items, quick editing/deletion, and one-click transfer to stock. I\'m also prioritizing an aggregated price and helpful statistics, along with a fast manual add form featuring categories and catalog search. The left/bottom side needs a quiet \"Quick Pantry Glance\" widget, a compact display of pantry stock status with quick add buttons. I\'m looking closely at `src/components/ShoppingBranchView.tsx`.\n\n\n**Designing Split-View Experience**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the split-view design, focusing on a fluid user experience. The desktop view will feature a 2-column layout, and I\'m ensuring mobile adapts with tabs for the checklist and pantry glance. The pantry widget will display items by slot, with quick add to the shopping list. The shopping checklist will include checkboxes, copy actions, stock transfer, batch actions, and a quick add form.\n\n\n"
