    thinking: "**Examining Authentication State**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how the authentication state, specifically `isAuthLoading` and `authInitialized`, are handled within `PantryContext`. My primary concern is the user experience upon visiting the app. I\'m exploring the behavior of `authLoading` transitioning from `true` to completion after `supabase.auth.getSession()` or `getCurrentUser()` completes. If no user is found and loading is false, I intend to show a clear dedicated section.\n\n\n**Designing Auth UI**\n\nI\'ve shifted my attention to the user interface for authentication. I\'m building a full-screen authentication guard, complete with a login and registration screen. It will support Hebrew, email/password login via Supabase, with an optional fast signup option. Error alerts and modern styling are top priorities. I\'m focusing on the `/src/components/AuthScreen.tsx` design, a clean Hebrew card with Supabase Auth integration, including \"\327\233\327\240\327\231\327\241\327\224 \327\234\327\236\327\242\327\250\327\233\327\252\" (Sign In), \"\327\224\327\250\327\251\327\236\327\224 \327\234\327\236\327\242\327\250\327\233\327\252\" (Sign Up) and \"\327\247\327\231\327\251\327\225\327\250 \327\247\327\241\327\235\" (Magic Link) tabs, and email/password input validation.\n\n\n"
