    thinking: "**Refining Error Handling**\n\nI\'m now diving into `src/components/AuthScreen.tsx` to optimize the sign-up and sign-in experiences. The current focus is on translating detailed error messages into clear, user-friendly Hebrew. For instance, \"User already registered\" will become \"\327\236\327\251\327\252\327\236\327\251 \327\226\327\224 \327\233\327\221\327\250 \327\250\327\251\327\225\327\235\". I\'m aiming for seamless authentication with robust error handling.\n\n\n**Translating Error Messages**\n\nI\'ve expanded error message translations for user authentication. The goal is clear, actionable Hebrew messaging. I\'ve translated: \"User already registered\" into a user-friendly message with a quick link to the login tab. The translation for password length, email rate limits, unconfirmed emails, disabled signups, and invalid credentials are ready as well. I\'m focusing on user-centered explanations and solutions for any raw error.\n\n\n"
