  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Sign-Up Behavior**\n\nOkay, so I\'m currently focused on how Supabase\'s `signUp` method behaves when email confirmation is enabled. My recent observation is that when `supabase.auth.signUp()` runs, it returns a user object and a null session. This makes perfect sense; since email verification is required, there\'s no active session until the user confirms their email.\n\n\n**Refining Email Confirmation Flow**\n\nI\'ve been drilling down on the user experience after a successful Supabase signup with email confirmation. Crucially, `onAuthStateChange` doesn\'t emit `SIGNED_IN`, so the `currentUser` stays null in `PantryContext`. The user gets a \"account created\" message, but can\'t proceed. My proposed solution in `AuthScreen.tsx` aims for a smoother transition. If `signUp` returns `data.user` and `data.session` is null, I\'ll attempt an immediate `signInWithPassword`. If that fails with \"Email not confirmed\", a clear banner message will guide them.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 10
      nanos: 783518095
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
