  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Initiating Edit Functionality**\n\nI\'m currently focused on implementing a full edit mode within `ItemDetailModal.tsx`. My primary goal is to provide a user-friendly way to modify every field. I\'m thinking of an \"\327\242\327\250\327\231\327\233\327\252 \327\244\327\250\327\231\327\230\" button that would toggle between a display and edit mode, offering either a complete edit form or in-line editable inputs. I\'m starting with the `name` and `slot` fields.\n\n\n**Expanding Edit Features**\n\nI\'ve expanded the edit mode to include dropdowns for `slot` with seven specific options in Hebrew, and also a department selector. I\'m adding fields for `quantity` with number input, unit selection, and a `minThreshold` input with a helpful explanation. I\'m also thinking about an auto-updating `status` field.\n\n\n**Adding New Item Fields**\n\nI\'m now integrating new fields into the edit functionality. This includes barcode or SKU, an expiry date, price per unit, notes for location or usage, and the daily usage rate. I also plan to add a save button, which will instantly update Supabase, and a cancel button to exit edit mode.\n\n\n\n**Implementing New Item Details**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating new data points for new items. I need to include an estimated price per unit, and a location note field for the pantry. Additionally, I\'ll save to both the inventory state and Supabase using `addNewPantryItem(...)`.\n\n**Improving Add Item Buttons**\n\nI\'m working on prominent triggers to add new items. In `PhysicalRackView.tsx`, I\'ll include a top action button with the text \"+ \327\224\327\225\327\241\327\243 \327\244\327\250\327\231\327\230 \327\227\327\223\327\251 \327\234\327\236\327\226\327\225\327\225\327\224\" in the header. Also, each slot section header will display \"+ \327\224\327\225\327\241\327\243 \327\244\327\250\327\231\327\230 \327\234\327\241\327\234\327\225\327\230 \327\226\327\224\". For empty slots, I\'ll have a button labeled \"\327\224\327\225\327\241\327\243 \327\244\327\250\327\231\327\230 \327\250\327\220\327\251\327\225\327\237 \327\234\327\241\327\234\327\225\327\230 \327\226\327\224\".\n\n**Adding Threshold Alerts**\n\nI\'m making sure `updatePantryItem` and `quickStockChange` accurately compare quantity to the minimum threshold in `PantryContext.tsx`. If `quantity === 0`, the status is \'EMPTY\'; if `quantity <= minThreshold`, the status is \'LOW\'; otherwise, it\'s \'IN_STOCK\'. I also plan to add a visual badge on low or empty cards in `PhysicalRackView.tsx` with a quick add button.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 13
      nanos: 215512545
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
